      "side": 1,
      "message": "I understand that the code-path nerfs the outgoing message, my question is if the caller who invoked thermal_genl_send_event should be made aware of this by means of the return code or not. A caller in this version will never know if their message was actually sent, or if higher powers decided this should not be sent. \n\nI am not strongly advocating to not use 0, I can see how this should be abstracted away from the caller. I just want to make sure its the intended behavior that the caller will perceive a blocked message in the same way as a message that was sent.",
